 In general $(R,+,dot):$ ring $==> (R,+):$ group with unit = $0_R.$

- $R$ ring $==> R^times$ is a group w.r.t. multiplication, unit = $1_R.$

*Notation* $quad G$ group, $S subset G$ as subset, $ angle.l S angle.r :={s_1^(a_1) dots s_n^(a_n) | n in ZZ_(>=0),s_i in S, a_i in ZZ} subset G $ as subgroup, and is the smallest subgroup of $G$ containing $S.$

We say $S$ is a family of generators of $G,$ iff $angle.l S angle.r=G.$

*Examples* $quad$ $"S"(n)$ is generated by $s_i=(i quad i+1),$ $ZZ\/n ZZ$ is generated by $1+n ZZ.$ 

If $n>1,$ then $k+n ZZ$ generates $ZZ\/n ZZ<==>gcd(k,n)=1.$

